    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n11718" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀπείραστος</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>,
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>incapable of being tempted,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κακῶν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>Ep.Jac.</u>
					1.13
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>without experience,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τῶν ἀβουλήτων</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Alciphr.
					3.37
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>III.</b>
			<i>not experienced,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Gal.
				13.459
			</span></i>; <i>untried,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τέχνη</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Phld.
					<u>Rh.</u>
					1.45
				</span></i>
			
			<i><span class="en">
				S.
			</span></i></div>
